+## External AI consent (2026-10-03)
+
+Guideline 5.1.2(i) / APPI §28. Every server function that sends photos, words or typed text to an AI provider calls `assertAiConsent` (`src/lib/ai-consent.server.ts`) before anything is sent; the list is `AI_CONSENT_FUNCTIONS` in `src/lib/ai-consent.ts` (kept in step with iOS `AIConsent.aiFunctions`, checked by `ai-consent.test.ts`). Consent is stored in `ai_consents` (migration `20261003140000`, written by the service role only, users can read their own rows). The web asks in `AiConsentDialog` (signed-in users once after entering the app via `AiConsentAccountGate`, and whenever an AI call is refused with `AI_CONSENT_REQUIRED`; guests in the tutorial before the first AI call, stored on the device and asked again after sign-up). Settings has a card to review/withdraw. `/api/native-fn` (iOS) is enforced only when the request carries `AI-Consent-Version` or `AI_CONSENT_ENFORCE_NATIVE` is set, so older iOS builds keep working; see `docs/ios-spec/23-ai-consent.md` for `recordAiConsent` / `getAiConsent`. Until the migration is applied, the check passes (logged) so AI does not stop.
